    <custom_item>
      type        : SQL_POLICY
      description : "7.12 Ensure WebAuthn is Used for Phishing-Resistant Authentication Where Required"
      info        : "Where phishing-resistant authentication is required, configure MySQL Enterprise Edition to use WebAuthn for the appropriate factor. For MySQL 9.x, WebAuthn replaces older FIDO-focused wording and supports modern FIDO/FIDO2 authenticators.

WebAuthn provides stronger resistance to phishing and credential replay than password-only authentication.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Install and configure the MySQL Enterprise WebAuthn authentication support where required. Assign WebAuthn as an approved factor for designated accounts and review any passwordless deployments carefully before approval.

